My alternate proposal is to cleanup the url string manually before we create the URL object out of it 

```
        std::string cleaned(urlIn);
        cleaned.erase(std::remove_if(cleaned.begin(), cleaned.end(), [](char c) {
            return c == '<' || c == '>';
        }), cleaned.end());

        // Create a boost::urls::url_view from the cleaned URL
        boost::urls::url_view urlwithFragment(cleaned);
        // Check if the URL contains a fragment
        if (urlwithFragment.has_fragment()) {
            BMCWEB_LOG_CRITICAL("Fragment: {}", urlwithFragment.fragment());
        } else {
            BMCWEB_LOG_CRITICAL("No fragment present in the URL.");
        }
```

This works well and we are able to get the correct fragment. 

